WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.921
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.221 --> 00:00:09.304
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.604 --> 00:00:18.908
Unit eight: B1 Preliminary: Writing Email and Story or Article. Today you will write a clear email and a story or article of about 100 words.

4
00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:21.954
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.912
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.565
Email.

7
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.875
Email means a message sent online.

8
00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:33.413
Write an email to a friend.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:36.251
Your turn. Say: Email.

10
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:39.846
Email.

11
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:41.341
Greeting.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.651
Greeting means the first words of a message.

13
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.611
Dear Anna is a greeting.

14
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:49.393
Your turn. Say: Greeting.

15
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:53.281
Greeting.

16
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:54.902
Article.

17
00:00:55.917 --> 00:00:58.671
Article means a piece of writing in a magazine.

18
00:00:59.283 --> 00:01:01.608
Write an article for a school magazine.

19
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:05.043
Your turn. Say: Article.

20
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.785
Article.

21
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.365
Story.

22
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.512
Story means a text about events.

23
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.222
Write a story.

24
00:01:15.817 --> 00:01:18.376
Your turn. Say: Story.

25
00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:22.246
Story.

26
00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:23.915
Paragraph.

27
00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.880
Paragraph means a section of text about one idea.

28
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:30.169
Write two paragraphs.

29
00:01:30.783 --> 00:01:33.227
Your turn. Say: Paragraph.

30
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.149
Paragraph.

31
00:01:37.883 --> 00:01:38.861
Opinion.

32
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.455
Opinion means what you think.

33
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.330
Give your opinion.

34
00:01:43.917 --> 00:01:46.348
Your turn. Say: Opinion.

35
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.224
Opinion.

36
00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:52.460
Past continuous.

37
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.936
Past continuous means a tense for background actions.

38
00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.690
It was raining.

39
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:02.261
Your turn. Say: Past continuous.

40
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.612
Past continuous.

41
00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.409
Word count.

42
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:11.602
Word count means the number of words.

43
00:02:12.217 --> 00:02:13.508
Check the word count.

44
00:02:14.117 --> 00:02:16.548
Your turn. Say: Word count.

45
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.540
Word count.

46
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:24.822
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.683 --> 00:02:28.426
Visal, what are the two writing tasks?

48
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:40.412
In Part 1 you write an email of about a hundred words and answer all the points in the question. In Part 2 you choose between an article and a story.

49
00:02:41.517 --> 00:02:43.110
How do I write a good email?

50
00:02:44.217 --> 00:02:53.951
Begin with Hi or Dear, answer every point with details, and end politely. Use simple linking words like because, but and so.

51
00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.026
How about the story or article?

52
00:02:58.117 --> 00:03:07.340
For a story, use past tenses and a clear beginning, middle and end. For an article, give your opinion with examples and use a lively title.

53
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.279
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:14.916
Grammar focus: Strategy: cover the points, plan, check.

55
00:03:15.216 --> 00:03:16.426
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.117 --> 00:03:19.360
It was raining when I arrived at the station.

57
00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:23.120
In my opinion, a school trip is good for learning.

58
00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:31.061
Read the task carefully and cover every point. Plan your paragraphs, use a variety of tenses and check the grammar and word count.

59
00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:35.862
Be careful! Don't say: I write more than 200 words.

60
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.322
Say: I write about 100 words.

61
00:03:40.622 --> 00:03:42.192
Respect the word count.

62
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.490
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.963
An Email to a Friend.

64
00:03:48.263 --> 00:03:51.377
Sophea must write to a friend about a school trip.

65
00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.458
She begins with Hi Anna and thanks her for the invitation.

66
00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.894
She answers all three points about the date, the place and the cost.

67
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.503
She uses because and so to link her ideas.

68
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.521
At the end she checks her grammar and spelling.

69
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:12.322
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:13.183 --> 00:04:16.030
The email in Part 1 is about blank words.

71
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:20.471
A, 1000. B, 10. C, 100.

72
00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.824
The answer is C: 100.

73
00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:29.157
You must answer blank in the task.

74
00:04:29.457 --> 00:04:33.703
A, every point. B, one point. C, no points.

75
00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.858
The answer is A: every point.

76
00:04:41.017 --> 00:04:43.376
The past continuous is used for blank.

77
00:04:43.676 --> 00:04:47.852
A, commands. B, background actions. C, future plans.

78
00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.479
The answer is B: background actions.

79
00:04:55.617 --> 00:04:58.081
A story needs a beginning, middle and blank.

80
00:04:58.381 --> 00:05:01.918
A, title only. B, picture. C, end.

81
00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.571
The answer is C: end.

82
00:05:08.717 --> 00:05:10.507
What does Sophea check at the end?

83
00:05:10.807 --> 00:05:14.902
A, grammar and spelling. B, her bag. C, the weather.

84
00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:21.012
The answer is A: grammar and spelling.

85
00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.561
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:26.417 --> 00:05:28.985
How do you write a good email in B1 Preliminary?

87
00:05:37.783 --> 00:05:39.760
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:53.674
I read the question and underline every point that I must answer. I begin with a greeting, answer each point with details and finish politely. At the end I check my grammar, spelling and word count.

89
00:05:53.974 --> 00:05:55.626
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:56.517 --> 00:06:01.688
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: cover the points, plan, check.

91
00:06:01.988 --> 00:06:06.185
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:06:06.485 --> 00:06:08.800
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

93
00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:12.531
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

